        "title": "Conversation lifecycle: archive, rename, pin, and snooze",
        "summary": "The session list gained a full lifecycle toolkit backed by server-side state, so organizing chats now follows users across Aura clients.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Conversations can be archived and restored from the sessions list and Sidekick context menu, moving them out of the active date buckets without deleting the transcript; the status is server-backed so it syncs across clients.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "282eab40986b2cdc42cf69936109d5b11846dd0b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Sessions now have editable titles with an inline rename flow, validated up to 120 characters and persisted through a new PUT endpoint on the agents API.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0abff91d34b884bdbddaf71f55915f39b56bff3c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Users can pin conversations to the top of the list, with pin state persisted per session and surfaced in both the chat left panel and the agent info Chats tab.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8cf6fb283db5c97c2c4cd07b1408b52e1302532f"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "New snooze action temporarily hides a conversation until a chosen future time (or wakes it immediately), with server-side validation rejecting past timestamps and missing wake targets.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8115727bb1d09e5cf5bff4a7c559f2d9cad01d13"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Chat composer now persists unfinished drafts, guards oversized prompts with an inline 'Remove N characters to send' hint that keeps the textarea editable while disabling send, and adds a global prompt shelf saved via Cmd+S on desktop and a dedicated button on mobile.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6e9c37ca6480c78d59af1e8d646481fbc4e109b5",
              "352081d5ddfde3fad7c220f5f6ce04c20cd98ef2",
              "694f2056d7ef98bb60d38846745fa68019a0567e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Preview builds now prefer local workspace routing when the client can reach it, keeping local sessions off the remote tunnel while still honoring explicitly selected remote instances for remote-only clients.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "7c0c1fdd74b726874914a645597d63a8be95ea53"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
